# Profile entry for dpv-odrl:Location over DPV Locations, the containment slice.
#
# The operand is dpv-odrl:Location, the DPV-ODRL left operand for places
# drawn from DPV. DPV-ODRL places it below odrl:spatial, the operand the
# GeoNames profile binds. The sort is mer in all three profiles. What
# differs between them is the resource: which file, and which of the
# relations in that file the binding reads.  That is what it means for the
# meaning to belong to the binding rather than to the operand.
#
# The resource is containment only.  A constraint whose right
# operand is a supranational union does not ground under this
# profile: the union edges are membership, and this reading does
# not take them as containment.
#
# This binding reads skos:sameAs as identity.  DPV 2.3 uses this property,
# which SKOS does not define, for 30 pairs; owl:sameAs would be read the
# same way.  The BQ and SJ pairs merge different places: BQ with NL-BQ1,
# NL-BQ2 and NL-BQ3, and SJ with NO-21 and NO-22, so the islands of each
# group are one concept here.
# Issues filed with DPV: UPSTREAM-ISSUES.md.
# No test case relies on these merges.

@prefix dpv-odrl: <https://w3id.org/dpv/mappings/odrl#> .
@prefix bind: <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/binding#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/profile/> .

ex:b-spatial-dpvloc-geo a bind:OperandBinding ;
    rdfs:label "DPV Locations, territorial reading: places and their parts"@en ;
    bind:leftOperand dpv-odrl:Location ;
    bind:sort bind:mer ;
    bind:resource <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/dpv-loc-geo> ;
    bind:grounding bind:sliceMembership .
